Diagnostic artifact collector

This image executes only immutable, reviewed recipes. See:
  /usr/share/breakglass/runbooks/upstream/diagnostic-artifact-collection/README.md
  /usr/share/breakglass/runbooks/upstream/diagnostic-artifact-collection/RUNBOOK.md

Optional internal documentation (read-only, never executed):
  /usr/share/breakglass/runbooks/internal

Recipes:
  system-summary.v1 (detailLevel basic|extended, 2m, 16 MiB)
  crashdump-collection.v1 (nodeName + maxAgeMinutes, 15m, 512 MiB)
The crashdump recipe requires its controller host-path capability; both
recipes require session upload-egress. No arbitrary commands, paths, mounts,
credentials, or storage fallback are accepted.

The uploader consumes /output/artifact.tar.gz only after /output/artifact.ready
exists. The archive is bounded, private, and never overwrites an output.
The collector is offline; only the UID 65532 uploader connects to the exact
controller endpoint using the bundled verified CA roots. Crashdump collection
may run as UID 0 with all capabilities dropped when host files require it.
